hadiths[69]{hadithnumber,text}:
"579","Jabir (RAA) narrated that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) prohibited whitening a grave with plaster, to sit on it or to build over it (such as a dome).’ Related by Muslim."
"580","‘Amir bin Rabi’Ah (RAA) narrated that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) prayed over ‘Uthman bin Madh’un, then went to the grave and sprinkled three handfuls of soil while he was standing.’ Related by Ad-Darqutni."
"581","‘Uthman Ibn ‘Affan (RAA) narrated, ‘Whenever the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) finished the burial of the dead, he would stand by the grave and say, “Seek forgiveness for your brother and pray for him to be steadfast, because he is now being questioned.” Related by Abu Dawud. Al-Hakim graded it as Sahih."
"582","Ibn Khuzaimah has reported it similarly from Ibn 'Abbas (RA)."
"583","At-Tabarani Related A similar Hadith on the authority of Abu Umamah on the authority of the Prophet (ﷺ)."
"584","“I had forbidden you to visit graves, but now you may visit them.” Related by Muslim. At-Tirmidhi added the following, “It will remind you of the Here-after.\""585"""
"585","On his authority: A woman from Juhaynah came to the Prophet (ﷺ) and said: ""My mother vowed to perform Hajj, but she did not perform Hajj until she died. Should I perform Hajj on her behalf?"" He said: ""Yes, perform Hajj on her behalf. Do you not see that if your mother had a debt, you would pay it off? Fulfill the debt owed to Allah, for Allah is more deserving of fulfillment."" Narrated by Al-Bukhari."
"586","Abu Hurairah (RAA) narrated that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) cursed the women who frequently visit the graves. Related At-Tirmidhi and Ibn Hibban graded it as Sahih."
"587","Abu Sa'id Al-Khudri (RAA) narrated that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) cursed the wailing women and those who listen to them. Related by Abu Dawud."
"588","Umm ‘Atiyah (RAA) narrated that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) made us pledge that we will not wail. Agreed upon."
"589","Ibn ’Umar (RAA) narrated that the Messenger of Allah said, “A dead person is tormented in his grave by the wailing for him.” Agreed upon."
"590","Al-Bukhari and Muslim transmitted a similar narration on the authority of Al·Mughirah bin Shu'bah."
"591","Anas (RAA) narrated Attended the burial of one of the daughters of the Prophet (ﷺ) He was sitting by the side of the grave and his eyes were shedding tears.’ Related by Al-Bukhari."
"592","\Do not bury your dead during the night unless you have to do so.\"" Related by Ibn Majah. Muslim reported a similar narration"
"593","“Prepare some food for the family of Ja’far, for what has befallen them is keeping them preoccupied.” Related by the five lmams except for An-Nasa’i."
"594","Sulaiman bin Buraidah narrated on the authority of his father (RAA) that the Prophet (ﷺ) taught us that when we visit graves we should say, “Peace be upon you, O believing men and women, O dwellers of this place. Certainly, Allah willing, we will join you. We supplicate to Allah to grant us and you well being.” Related by Muslim."
"595","Ibn ‘Abbas (RAA) narrated, ‘Once the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) passed by some graves in Madinah. He turned his face toward them saying, “Peace be upon you, O dwellers of these graves. May Allah forgive you and us. You have preceded us, and we are following your trail.\ Related by At-Tirmidhi"
"596","“Do not speak badly of the dead, they have already seen the result of (the deeds) that they sent on before them.” Related by Al·Bukhari."
"597","At-Tirmidhi Related a similar narration on the authority of Al-Mughirah bin Shu’bah, and he added, \Thus you will be offending the living (i.e. if you curse their dead).\"""""
"598","It was narrated from Hazrat Uthman bin Affan, may Allah be pleased with him, that the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: \The one who is in ihram should marry himself"
"599","On the authority of Hazrat Abu Qatadah Ansari... in the story of his hunting a wild donkey while he was not wearing Ihram... It was narrated that the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, said to his Companions who were in Ihram: \Did any of you command him or give him any indication?\"" They said: No. He said: \""Eat what is left of his flesh.\"" (Bukhari and Muslim)."""
"600","It is narrated from Hazrat Saab bin Jathama Laithi that he sent a wild donkey as a gift to the Messenger of Allah, may Allah bless him and grant him peace, while he was in the position of \Abuwa\"" or \""Wadaan\"". He returned it to them and said: \""We returned it only because we are in Ihram.\"" (Bukhari and Muslim)."""
"601","On the authority of Hazrat Aisha, the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: \Five animals are so dangerous that they can be killed inside the Haram and outside the Haram (anywhere). And they are: the scorpion"
"602","It was narrated on the authority of Hazrat Abdullah bin Abbas that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) wore a horn in the state of Ihram. (Bukhari and Muslim)"
"603","It was narrated from Hazrat Ka'b bin Ajrah (RA) that I was carried to the Messenger of Allah (PBUH) while lice were falling on my face. He said: \I did not think that the disease would have brought you to the state that I see.\"" Do you have a goat?” I said: No. He said: \""Fast for three days or feed six poor people.\"" Give half to every poor person.” (Bukhari and Muslim)"""
"604","It was narrated from Hazrat Abu Huraira that when Allah granted victory to His Messenger (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) over Makkah, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) stood among the people. And research before me Makkah was not lawful for anyone. An hour of the day has been made lawful for me, and certainly it will not be lawful for anyone after me, so it should not be hunted, nor should any of its thorns be pierced, and it is not lawful to pick up its fallen object except for the one who announces it. And whoever has a man killed, he has the option of one of the two things that is better. Allow azhar (a type of grass' i.e. its cutting) because we use it in our graves and in our homes. So he said: \Except for Azhar.\"" (It is permissible to cut it.) (Bukhari and Muslim)."""
"605","On the authority of Hazrat Abdullah bin Zayd bin Asim, the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: \Undoubtedly"
"606","On the authority of Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Madinah is a sanctuary from Mount Ayr to Mount Thor.” (Narrated by Muslim)."
"607","It was narrated from Hazrat Jabir bin Abdullah (RA) that the Messenger of Allah (PBUH) performed Hajj and we went out with him until we reached Dhul-Halifa, then Asma bint Umays (RA) gave birth to a child. He said: \Take a bath and put on a diaper and put on Ihram.\"" \""The Messenger of Allah"
"608","It is narrated from Hazrat Khuzima bin Thabit (RA) that when the Prophet (PBUH) would finish saying Talbiyah during Hajj or Umrah, he would seek Allah's permission and Paradise and seek refuge from the Fire with His mercy. (It was narrated by Imam Shafi'i, may God have mercy on him, with a weak chain of transmission.)"
"609","On the authority of Hazrat Jabir, may Allah be pleased with him, the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: \I have sacrificed at this place"
"610","It was narrated from Hazrat Aisha that when the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) entered Makkah (for Hajj), he entered from the upper part of Makkah and left from its lower part. (Bukhari and Muslim)"
"611","It is narrated from Hazrat Ibn Umar that whenever he came to Makkah, he would spend the night in Dhu Tuwa until morning and perform ghusl and would say that the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, used to do the same. (Bukhari and Muslim)"
"612","It was narrated from Hazrat Ibn Abbas that he used to kiss the Black Stone and prostrate on it. (It has been narrated by al-Hakim in marfoo and by Bayhaqi)."
"613","It was narrated from Hazrat Ibn Abbas (RA) that the Prophet (SAW) ordered his companions to run lightly in three circles and walk four circles as usual and walk between the two legs. (Bukhari and Muslim)"
"614","It was narrated from Hazrat Abdullah bin Umar (RA) that whenever he performed Tawaf Qadum (First Tawaf) of the House of Allah, he would walk like a wrestler in the first three circles and walk slowly in the (remaining) four. In another hadith, Abdullah bin Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates the actions of the Messenger of Allah (may peace be upon him) and says: I saw the Messenger of Allah (may peace be upon him) that whenever he performed Tawaf for Hajj or Umrah, he would perform the first three circumambulations at a fast pace and walk slowly during the remaining four. (Bukhari and Muslim)"
"615","It was narrated on the authority of Hazrat Abdullah bin Umar, that I did not see the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, touch any member of the House of Allah except the two Yemeni members. (Narrated by Muslim.)"
"616","It is narrated from Hazrat Umar that he kissed the black stone and said: I know very well that you are a stone. So he does not own any kind of profit or loss. If I had not seen the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) kissing you, I would never have kissed you. (Bukhari and Muslim)"
"617","It was narrated from Hazrat Abu Tufail (RA) that I saw the Messenger of Allah (PBUH) circumambulating the House of Allah. You used to touch the black stone with the stick you had and then kiss the stick. (Narrated by Muslim.)"
"618","It is narrated from Hazrat Ya'ila bin Umayyah that the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, performed Tawaf in a green cloak, which he took out from his right armpit and put on his left shoulder. (It has been narrated by all five except Nasa'i and Tirmidhi has declared it Sahih.)"
"619","It was narrated from Hazrat Anas (may Allah be pleased with him) that some of us used to say Talbiyah, which was not considered bad, and some of us used to say Takbeer, which was also not considered bad. (Bukhari and Muslim)"
"620","On the authority of Hazrat Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with him, he said that the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, sent me from Muzdalifah (toward Mina) at night with the baggage of travelers or he said with the weak. (Bukhari and Muslim)"
"621","It is narrated from Hazrat Aisha (RA) that Hazrat Saudah (RA) asked Rasulullah (SAW) for permission to return before him on the night of Muzdalifah, and (she asked for this permission because) she was heavy-bodied. You gave them permission. (Bukhari and Muslim)"
"622","On the authority of Hazrat Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with him, the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, said to us: \Do not throw stones before sunrise.\"""""
"623","It was narrated from Hazrat Aisha that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) had sent Umm Salama (may Allah be pleased with him) before the night of sacrifice. (It was narrated by Abu Dawud and its authenticity is on the condition of Muslim.)"
"624","On the authority of Hazrat Urwah bin Mudars, may Allah be pleased with him, the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Whoever joins us in this prayer, i.e. Muzdalifah (Fajr prayer) and stands with us until we have marched, and before that he has stood in Arafat during the night or day, then his Hajj has been completed and he has removed his mail.” (Narrated by all five and Tirmidhi and Ibn Khazima has declared it to be correct.)"
"625","Hazrat Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that the polytheists used to return (from Muzdalifah) after sunrise and say: O Sabir (Mountain!), lighten up. But the Prophet opposed them and left before sunrise. (Narrated by Bukhari.)"
"626","It was narrated from both Hazrat Ibn Abbas and Usama bin Zayd that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to say talbiyah until he pelted the Jumrah of Aqaba with stones. (Narrated by Bukhari.)"
"627","It is narrated on the authority of Hazrat Abdullah bin Masoud that he placed Baitullah on his left side and Mina on his right side and hit the Jamrah with seven pebbles and said that this is the standing place of the person on whom Surah Baqarah was revealed. (Bukhari and Muslim)"
"628","It was narrated from Hazrat Jabir (may Allah be pleased with him) that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) threw pebbles at the time of Chasht on the Day of Sacrifice of Jumrah, and after that day after sunset (he continued to throw pebbles) (Narrated by Muslim)."
"629","It was narrated from Hazrat Ibn Umar (RA) that he used to throw seven pebbles at the nearest Jamra (of Masjid al-Khaif) and say Takbeer while hitting each pebble. While going, he would raise both his hands and pray for a long time. After that, they used to hit Jumrah Aqaba with pebbles from the lower part of the valley, but did not stay there, then came back. Hazrat Ibn Umar Radiyallahu Anhuma narrated that I saw the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, do the same. (Narrated by Bukhari.)"
"630","It is narrated from Hazrat Ibn Umar (RA) that the Messenger of Allah (PBUH) said: “God! Have mercy on those who shave their heads (pilgrims).” The Companions said: O Messenger of Allah! Also on the barbers. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said for the third time: “Have mercy on those who cut their hair.” (Bukhari and Muslim)"
"631","It was narrated from Hazrat Abdullah bin Amr bin As, that the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, stood at a place during Hajj al-Wada. The Companions of the Prophet (may God bless him and grant him peace) started asking him questions. Someone said: I did not know, so I performed hijamat before the sacrifice. He said to him: \Sacrifice now. There is no harm.\"" And a man said"
"632","It is narrated from Hazrat Masoor bin Mukharama that the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, offered sacrifice before performing cupping and ordered his companions to do the same. (Narrated by Bukhari.)"
"633","It is narrated from Hazrat Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her) that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: “When you throw pebbles and shave your head, perfumes and all other things become lawful for you except wives.”"
"634","On the authority of Hazrat Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with him, the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: \It is not for women to shave their heads"
"635","It is narrated from Hazrat Ibn Umar (RA) that Hazrat Abbas bin Abdul Muttalib (RA) asked the Messenger of Allah (SAW) for permission to spend the nights of Mina in Makkah so that he could drink Zamzam water, so he gave him permission. (Bukhari and Muslim)"
"636","It was narrated from Hazrat Asim bin Udi (may Allah be pleased with him) that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) allowed the camel herders to spend the night outside Mina to throw pebbles on the day of sacrifice, then throw pebbles on the day of sacrifice, then throw pebbles for two days (one day together) on the day of sacrifice, and then throw pebbles on the day of the coach. (It has been narrated by all five and has been declared authentic by Tirmidhi and Ibn Hibban.)"
"637","It is narrated from Hazrat Abu Bakra (RA) that the Messenger of Allah (PBUH) gave us a sermon on the Day of Sacrifice. And mentioned all the hadith. (Bukhari and Muslim)"
"638","It was narrated from Hazrat Sara bint Nabahan (RA) that the Messenger of Allah (PBUH) gave us a sermon on the Day of the Heads and said: \Isn't this day the middle day of the days of Tashreeq?\"" and mentioned the entire hadith. (It was narrated by Abu Dawud with a hasan chain of transmission.)"""
"639","On the authority of Hazrat Aisha, the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to her: “To circumambulate your House of Allah and to try to walk between Safa and Marwah is enough for your Hajj and your Umrah.” (Narrated by Muslim)."
"640","It is narrated from Hazrat Ibn Abbas (RA) that the Prophet (PBUH) did not perform the seven rounds of Tawaf Afazah. (It has been narrated by all five except Tirmidhi and Hakim has declared it Sahih.)"
"641","It was narrated from Anas (may Allah be pleased with him) that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prayed Zuhr, Asr, Maghrib and Isha in Muhsab, then slept a little. Then (later) they rode towards the House of Allah and circumambulated it. (Narrated by Bukhari.)"
"642","It was narrated from Hazrat Aisha that she did not stay at Abtah (Muhasab) and she used to say that the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, stayed at this place because it was easier to return from here. (Narrated by Muslim)."
"643","It is narrated from Hazrat Ibn Abbas (RA) that the Messenger of Allah (PBUH) ordered the people that their last act should be circumambulation of the House of Allah, but it has been reduced for menstruating women. (Bukhari and Muslim)"
"644","On the authority of Hazrat Ibn Zubair, may Allah be pleased with him, the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: \The reward of offering one prayer in this mosque of mine is a thousand times greater than offering prayers in other mosques"
"645","It was narrated on the authority of Hazrat Ibn Abbas that when the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was stopped (at Hudaybiyah), he shaved his head, married his wives and slaughtered sacrificial animals, then performed Umrah the following year. (Narrated by Bukhari.)"
"646","It is narrated from Hazrat Aisha that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) visited Zubayah bint Zubair bin Abdul Muttalib. He said: O Messenger of Allah! I intend to perform Hajj but I am ill. Then the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: \Perform Hajj and make a condition that the place where I will open my Ihram will be where"
"647","Hazrat Ikramah narrated from Hajjaj bin Amr Ansari that the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: \If a person breaks a bone or becomes lame"
